@@ ## Step 2 — Read critically, then write the report
 Work through the paper in order. For each section, ask the reviewer's core question, then report findings using the template below.
+
+Before writing, do a **contradiction sweep** and list every clash you find as a concern:
+- Methods vs Limitations (e.g. "assessors were blinded" vs "blinding was not possible").
+- Data-analysis section vs Results (e.g. "descriptive analysis only" vs "no statistically significant difference").
+- Results vs Discussion wording (e.g. 26% attrition described as "a low dropout rate").
+- Abstract group labels vs table labels (Group I/II vs A/B; is each mapped to a material?).

@@ ## Risk of bias
-[Apply the design-appropriate tool; rate each domain Low / Some concerns / High with a one-line justification]
+[Apply the design-appropriate tool. State the outcome assessed. Give a table:
+| Domain | Judgement | Reason (quote or cite the paper) |
+and an **Overall** row using the tool's own rule.]

