@@ ## Dental-specific RCT traps
 - **Split-mouth designs** treat both sides of one mouth — ...
+- **Fixed treatment order in split-mouth.** If one material is always placed first (e.g. "MTA, then Biodentine on the opposite tooth after 1 week"), the order isn't randomized. Unless the side was randomized and that is reported, rate RoB 2 Domain 1 **High**. Also check that "randomly assigned to two groups" makes sense when every patient receives both.

--- paper-critic/references/stats-and-dental.md
+++ paper-critic/references/stats-and-dental.md
@@ ## Reporting quality
+- **Reconcile every table across timepoints.** Counts at a later visit can't exceed the earlier visit. In split-mouth or crossover designs both arms must have the same patient n at every visit. Recompute row and column totals against the stated n; any mismatch is a data-integrity concern (usually major).
